12783300]],"about":{"what":"Lam Research (LRCX). This chart runs from Jun 24, 2025 to Oct 29, 2025.","setup":"The stock rose about 36% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $108.02 and pulling back 13% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Sep 11, 2025 it closed at $115.58, its first close above the base high of $107.81. Volume that day was 20.3M shares, 2.09x the prior 10-day average of 9.7M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $160.67, and the chart ends at $160.67.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}